Going to create the Test2::Harness2 module which is going to be an interface into the harness service, and makes it possible to connect to an dlaunch a service.

Namespaces:

Test2::Harness2
    API for starting and/or connecting to a harness service, queing jobs, etc

    my $t2h2 = Test2::Harness2->new(%specs)
    my $t2h2 = Test2::Harness2->connect(%info)

    new() creates a new harness, it will either need or vivify a workdir, a harness service class (or subclass), default to 'Test2::Harness2::Service::Harness'; Workdir would default to a tempdir like $TMPDIR/t2h2-$USER-$PROJECT. project is a required argument, no guessing or default.

Test2::Harness2::Role::Service
    Role with common functionality for all services
    Always starts via a collector
    Optional run_uuid, services are either global or run-based
    unique name per run or global (no 2 global services can have the same name, no 2 services for a specific run can have the same name, but a run service and a different runs service may, as well a run service may have the same name as a global service)
    Need a unix socket, usually $workdir/service_name.socket, or $workdir/$run_ord/service_name.socket. the run_ord is the numeric order of the runs based on order they were queued, starting with 1. WE use run_ord instead of uuid because of unix socket filename length limits.
    Has a loop
        - Reap children
        - accept socket connections
        - handle and respond to socket requests

Test2::Harness2::Service::Harness
    The main harness service
    Has a scheduler instance
    accepts requests from clients to queue runs (which also adds requesting client to the proxy list in the monitor to get state updates for global and run-specific collectors)
    Additional loop tasks:
        - get state changes from collectors and pass them to monitor
         - Forward monitor updates to any client that has asked to get them proxied
        - scheduler tick so it can kick off new jobs

Test2::Harness2::Scheduler
    Responsible for deciding when to start a run, when the run is done, when and how to kick off the jobs
    Initial version will just run 1 run and 1 test job at a time
    Monitor class is canonical way to tell when a job is done
    We will add support for resources and custom launchers later. For now launch a job using fork+exec to start the collector and the test job under the collector


Other notes:
Runs and jobs both get uuids run_uuid, and job_uuid. They can be passed in when calling queue_jobs, or they can be vivified when missing.
Collector events files will be written to these locations:
    $workdir/service_name.jsonl.zst
    $workdir/$run_ord/service_name.jsonl.zst
    $workdir/$run_ord/$job_ord/$job_try.jsonl.zst  (job tries numerical starting at 1, for now jobs only get 1 try, we will implement retry later)


